WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.285
Frank and Lisa were visiting their grandparents.

2
00:00:03.286 --> 00:00:06.023
"Get dressed and come down to breakfast.

3
00:00:06.024 --> 00:00:13.335
Also, find your bathing suits because we'll be swimming at the lake," said Mom.

4
00:00:13.336 --> 00:00:16.788
Frank couldn't find his bathing suit.

5
00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:21.331
"Mom told you to pack your bathing suit," scolded Lisa.

6
00:00:21.332 --> 00:00:24.657
"I guess you won't be going swimming today."

7
00:00:24.658 --> 00:00:27.809
"Be quiet!" said Frank.

8
00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:34.230
"I can wear my shorts to swim, as long as I bring an extra pair."

9
00:00:34.231 --> 00:00:40.728
"Lisa! Frank! Your breakfast is getting cold," called their grandma.

10
00:00:40.729 --> 00:00:44.577
"We're coming!" answered Lisa.

11
00:00:44.578 --> 00:00:50.136
"Found it!" shouted Frank happily.

12
00:00:50.137 --> 00:00:54.463
"Found—? Frank, this room is a mess!

13
00:00:54.464 --> 00:00:59.247
Why are all your clothes on the floor?" asked Mom.

14
00:00:59.248 --> 00:01:04.368
"He couldn't find his bathing suit," said Lisa.

15
00:01:04.369 --> 00:01:11.028
"Frank, you must put your clothes away before you have breakfast," said Mom.

16
00:01:11.029 --> 00:01:17.257
"Yes, Mom," answered Frank.

17
00:01:17.258 --> 00:01:23.040
"How many pancakes can you eat?" asked Grandma at breakfast.

18
00:01:23.041 --> 00:01:26.300
"I can eat three," said Lisa.

19
00:01:26.301 --> 00:01:28.846
"Do you have maple syrup?"

20
00:01:28.847 --> 00:01:32.576
"Yes," replied Grandpa. "It's real.

21
00:01:32.577 --> 00:01:35.460
I made it this spring."

22
00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:40.559
"You made it? How?" asked Lisa.

23
00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.114
"Well, it takes a lot of work.

24
00:01:43.115 --> 00:01:50.999
But each spring, as the weather gets warmer, the sap begins to run in the maple trees."

25
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.831
"Sap?" asked Lisa with a mouthful of pancakes.

26
00:01:55.832 --> 00:02:00.385
"Sap is tree blood," said Grandpa.

27
00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:07.136
"Yuck," said Lisa. "Syrup is made from blood!"

28
00:02:07.137 --> 00:02:10.739
"Lisa, tree blood isn't like human blood.

29
00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:14.470
Tree blood, sap, is mostly water and sugar.

30
00:02:14.471 --> 00:02:19.804
After a long winter's nap, a tree needs a nice long drink of sweet water.

31
00:02:19.805 --> 00:02:28.735
In the spring I take some of the sweet water from the maple trees and make maple syrup."

32
00:02:28.736 --> 00:02:33.685
"Are there any pancakes left for me?" asked Frank.

33
00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:36.196
"Sure, there's plenty.

34
00:02:36.197 --> 00:02:39.609
How many can you eat?" asked Grandma.

35
00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:46.877
"I can eat three," said Frank. "Pass the syrup, please."

36
00:02:46.878 --> 00:02:50.354
"Where's Dad?" asked Frank.

37
00:02:50.355 --> 00:02:55.938
"Oh, he took the boat to the lake this morning to go fishing," answered Mom.

38
00:02:55.939 --> 00:03:02.472
"Really?" said Frank sadly. "Why didn't he take me?"

39
00:03:02.473 --> 00:03:10.119
"Because he got up really early, before the sun came up," said Grandma.

40
00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:13.019
"Here, have some fruit."

41
00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:16.502
"I want an apple," said Lisa.

42
00:03:16.503 --> 00:03:20.156
"Can I have a banana?" asked Frank.

43
00:03:20.157 --> 00:03:24.083
"Ouch! My tooth!" cried Lisa.

44
00:03:24.084 --> 00:03:27.542
"What's wrong?" asked Mom.

45
00:03:27.543 --> 00:03:31.494
"My, my tooth. It's loose.

46
00:03:31.495 --> 00:03:34.074
Will I have to go to the dentist?

47
00:03:34.075 --> 00:03:38.509
Will I miss our trip to the lake?" asked Lisa.

48
00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:42.832
"Lisa, calm down," said Mom.

49
00:03:42.833 --> 00:03:48.014
"Lisa, you're a big girl now," said Grandma.

50
00:03:48.015 --> 00:03:52.145
"A big girl because I have a cavity."

51
00:03:52.146 --> 00:03:56.440
"You don't have a cavity," said Mom, laughing.

52
00:03:56.441 --> 00:03:59.728
"You have a loose tooth."

53
00:03:59.729 --> 00:04:09.151
"Today," continued Grandma, "you're a big girl because you're losing your baby teeth."

54
00:04:09.152 --> 00:04:14.360
"I'm losing my teeth?" asked Lisa, very concerned.

55
00:04:14.361 --> 00:04:22.364
"Yes," said Mom, "but new, bigger teeth will grow in place of the ones you lose."

56
00:04:22.365 --> 00:04:28.704
"Your mother lost her teeth when she was your age," said Grandma.

57
00:04:28.705 --> 00:04:31.973
"Really?" asked Lisa.

58
00:04:31.974 --> 00:04:34.710
"Yes, really," said Grandpa.

59
00:04:34.711 --> 00:04:39.506
"But the best thing about losing your teeth is the tooth fairy."

60
00:04:39.507 --> 00:04:43.024
"The tooth fairy?" asked Lisa.

61
00:04:43.025 --> 00:04:48.545
"Yes, when your tooth falls out, you take it and place it under your pillow.

62
00:04:48.546 --> 00:04:52.079
While you are sleeping, the tooth fairy will take the tooth.

63
00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:57.527
In exchange, the tooth fairy will grant you one wish," said Grandpa.

64
00:04:57.528 --> 00:04:59.863
"When can I make a wish?

65
00:04:59.864 --> 00:05:04.131
When will my tooth fall out?" asked Lisa.

66
00:05:04.132 --> 00:05:08.674
"Maybe today. Maybe tomorrow," said Mom.

67
00:05:08.675 --> 00:05:12.649
"You can't rush nature," said Grandma.

68
00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:16.031
"It will come out when it's ready."

